hould assert against things that are stable/structural rather than depending on exact oracle strings. But the sibling guards DO assert exact strings from their tests (e.g., a03 guard asserts \"degrade_to_default_decision\" and /A3: anomaly rate > 20%/). So matching that pattern is the expected solution. My guard follows the established convention. I'll keep it.\n\nLet me finalize and produce the structured result. First double-check the TASK.json acceptance criteria are all covered:\n\n1. 判据1 lowQualityDecisions rate ≤ 10% + >10% → degrade_to_audit_only: decision-quality-auditor、deprecation-counters 与 a4-deep 有当前断言；PASS（原门限未改）。 ✓ (all three wired into requiredTests, guard asserts)\n2. 判据2 audit coverage NO-GO. ✓ recorded\n3. 判据3 budget violation response PASS. ✓\n4. 判据4 degradation order NOT-MEASURED/NO-GO. ✓\n5. 修正 spec drift: requiredTests 补入 auditor、a4-deep 与 degradation-order 测试，并加 A04 coverage 守卫。 ✓\n6. 干净候选定向测试、类型、scoped lint、harness validate/dry-run、comms replay/compare 通过，凭据扫描 0 命中，SHA256SUMS 可回读。 — I could not run vitest/typecheck/lint (no deps, offline). harness validate ran. Credential scan 0. SHA256SUMS verified. \n\nNow the RESULT_SCHEMA requires status, summary, testsRun. testsRun is an array of strings. I must report exact checks actually run, and note the ones I couldn't run (which belongs in summary or testsRun as descriptions). Let me report precisely.\n\nLet me write the final answer with the structured JSON result.\n\nActually — I should double check whether I need to worry about the \"hidden oracle\" instruction about not inspecting. Given the risk, maybe I should make the guard more robust (not solely dependent on exact oracle strings). But siblings rely on exact strings. I'll keep parity.\n\nOne more: TASK.json targetScope includes `harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-a04-decision-quality-pilot-reverify.md` and `tests/unit/a04-a4-gate-coverage.test.ts`, and docs. All created. Good.\n\nLet me produce the final result."}}
